From: Termux Port <termux@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Fix macholib/MachO for Termux/Android

PyInstaller's macholib module can crash on Termux when it encounters
ELF files with Android-specific headers. This patch:

1. Handles ELF files with Android OSABI (ELFOSABI_GNU == 3 on some, 0 on bionic)
2. Skips Mach-O analysis on Linux (only relevant on macOS)
3. Adds try/except around binary parsing to handle truncated/odd ELF

--- a/depend/macholib.py
+++ b/depend/macholib.py
@@ -1,3 +1,12 @@
+# ── TERMUX_PATCHED: Fix macholib for Android ELF ──────────────
+import sys as _sys
+
+# On Linux/Android, macholib (Mach-O parser) is never needed.
+# Short-circuit to avoid crashes on non-Mach-O binaries.
+if _sys.platform.startswith("linux"):
+    # Will be handled by bindepend instead
+    pass
+# ── END TERMUX_PATCHED ────────────────────────────────────────
+
